# Hopeful Initiate's cost removes two +1/+1 counters from among creatures you control (CR 118.3, 122.1): no other kind pays
# it. On turn 3 Bot1's Loch Mare has three -1/-1 counters and Bot2's Walking Ballista a +1/+1 counter, and Bot1 controls no
# creature with a +1/+1 counter, so the ability is not offered (it would be under a reading of "counters" of any kind). Bot1
# casts its own Walking Ballista with two +1/+1 counters; on turn 5 the choice of counters refuses one of Loch Mare's and one
# of Bot2's Ballista's, the Ballista's two pay, and the ability destroys Bot1's own Mox Jet. The Ballista, left 0/0, dies
# (CR 704.5f) as soon as the cost is paid, before the Mox Jet is destroyed; Loch Mare keeps its counters.

